[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2644448750","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/102370#issuecomment-2644448750","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/102370","id":2644448750,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6dnxXu","user":{"login":"matorin57","id":5014337,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUwMTQzMzc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5014337?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/matorin57","html_url":"https://github.com/matorin57","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matorin57/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matorin57/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matorin57/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matorin57/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matorin57/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matorin57/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matorin57/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matorin57/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matorin57/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-08T02:51:10Z","updated_at":"2025-02-08T03:07:50Z","body":"I was poking around and I was able to repro using an array of fonts. It seems  in `update_tree()` in `editor_inspector.cpp` the array isn't considered a resource and so its sub objects don't get checked to see if they match the filter, at line 3368\n\n\n```\n\t\t// Ignore properties that do not fit the filter.\n\t\tbool sub_inspector_use_filter = false;\n\t\tif (use_filter && !filter.is_empty()) {\n\t\t\tconst String property_path = property_prefix + (path.is_empty() ? \"\" : path + \"/\") + name_override;\n\t\t\tif (!_property_path_matches(property_path, filter, property_name_style)) {\n\t\t\t\tif (!sub_inspectors_enabled || p.hint != PROPERTY_HINT_RESOURCE_TYPE) {\n\t\t\t\t\tcontinue;\n\t\t\t\t}\n\n\t\t\t\tRef<Resource> res = object->get(p.name);\n\t\t\t\tif (res.is_null()) {\n\t\t\t\t\tcontinue;\n\t\t\t\t}\n\n\t\t\t\t// Check if the sub-resource has any properties that match the filter.\n\t\t\t\tif (!_resource_properties_matches(res, filter)) {\n\t\t\t\t\tcontinue;\n\t\t\t\t}\n\n\t\t\t\tsub_inspector_use_filter = true;\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t}\n```\nWhen debugging the array's property hint is of PROPERTY_HINT_TYPE_STRING.\n\nI'm guessing this will need some special case for Array's since it will need to grab the underlying type for each element and then check if its a resource and then run `_resource_properties_matches()` on that.\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2644448750/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2644457599","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/102370#issuecomment-2644457599","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/102370","id":2644457599,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6dnzh_","user":{"login":"matorin57","id":5014337,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUwMTQzMzc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5014337?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/matorin57","html_url":"https://github.com/matorin57","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matorin57/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matorin57/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matorin57/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matorin57/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matorin57/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matorin57/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matorin57/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matorin57/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matorin57/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-08T03:11:11Z","updated_at":"2025-02-08T03:11:11Z","body":"I imagine a similar issue will happen with dictionaries as well","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2644457599/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2645785557","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/102370#issuecomment-2645785557","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/102370","id":2645785557,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6ds3vV","user":{"login":"Dowsley","id":22419861,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyNDE5ODYx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/22419861?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dowsley","html_url":"https://github.com/Dowsley","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dowsley/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dowsley/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dowsley/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dowsley/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dowsley/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dowsley/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dowsley/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dowsley/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dowsley/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-08T15:30:51Z","updated_at":"2025-02-08T15:30:51Z","body":"> I imagine a similar issue will happen with dictionaries as well\n\nCan confirm:\n\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/0cbfff0a-192e-4467-a874-7fdda383f7eb)\n\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/eb2ef434-97cf-4022-895f-c74e047e6f53)\n\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/e53aba2f-dcf4-424d-ab46-db7b55e4a735)","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2645785557/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2645859830","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/102370#issuecomment-2645859830","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/102370","id":2645859830,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6dtJ32","user":{"login":"matorin57","id":5014337,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUwMTQzMzc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5014337?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/matorin57","html_url":"https://github.com/matorin57","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matorin57/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matorin57/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matorin57/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matorin57/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matorin57/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matorin57/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matorin57/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matorin57/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matorin57/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-08T17:19:32Z","updated_at":"2025-02-08T17:19:32Z","body":"So I'm playing around and wrote a total hack just to see if I could force it to show for my specific test with this code\n\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/61665f12-c6b9-403d-9165-0430199e03af)\n\nAnd now will show the array when its sub object but it doesn't expand the items inside the array to show the properties that match\n\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/046596c1-dfc7-470e-99b5-ddc7015b4aa0)\n\nI'm gonna keep poking around to see if I can get it to expand.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2645859830/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2645870549","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/102370#issuecomment-2645870549","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/102370","id":2645870549,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6dtMfV","user":{"login":"matorin57","id":5014337,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUwMTQzMzc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5014337?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/matorin57","html_url":"https://github.com/matorin57","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matorin57/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matorin57/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matorin57/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matorin57/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matorin57/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matorin57/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matorin57/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matorin57/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matorin57/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-08T17:46:21Z","updated_at":"2025-02-08T17:46:21Z","body":"To get it to expand it looks like it would require quite a few changes, it would need to parse deep into the arrays and dictionaries to get the potential editor plugins at the top of the loop (around 3034 if I'm reading correctly), and then in multiple places do that again or remember that we did that to then display and filter them and display them (around 3720). \n\nThis function is already quite long and quite complex and I'm wondering if a hack to try and tag that nesting info and propagate it through the function could be quite difficult and make it more difficult to add new things in the future.\n\nI wonder if a restructure could be useful here where based on property type/usage hints we dispatch to distinct helper functions that can return the valid editors (potentially already applying the filter) and then have this just handle displaying those editors and merging them into the ordered list.\n\n**However, I understand that such a proposal is not really a reasonable fix for this bug, especially a low priority one.** It would require a fairly big refactor of an important function and I am almost definitely missing some important semantics the function handles. \n\nI'll keep poking around to see if I can get it to expand reasonably without a refactor but would be interested in hearing y'alls ideas.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2645870549/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2646161783","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/102370#issuecomment-2646161783","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/102370","id":2646161783,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6duTl3","user":{"lo